WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.372 --> 00:00:14.355
"Zann's right," Perda thought.

2
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:16.236
"We have to find Mellis!"

3
00:00:16.256 --> 00:00:19.577
"Let's use a Uniting spell," she said.

4
00:00:19.597 --> 00:00:21.277
"Okay," Zann said.

5
00:00:21.297 --> 00:00:24.698
"Now that we know she's still on our side, it should work."

6
00:00:25.398 --> 00:00:26.879
Perda turned to Anso.

7
00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:28.899
"Stay here in the village, okay?

8
00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:31.200
Try to learn more about what's going on."

9
00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:33.717
Anso agreed and hurried off.

10
00:00:34.518 --> 00:00:36.520
"Let's join friction," Zann said.

11
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.062
"Uniting spells take a lot of energy."

12
00:00:40.143 --> 00:00:41.524
They rubbed their hands together.

13
00:00:42.245 --> 00:00:45.047
Perda pictured Mellis and murmured, "Unite!"

14
00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:50.171
She grabbed Zann's hand, and he grabbed Zing's wing as they were zapped away.

15
00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:52.753
They landed in an empty meadow.

16
00:00:52.773 --> 00:00:53.854
"Did it work?"

17
00:00:54.275 --> 00:00:54.935
Zann asked.

18
00:00:54.955 --> 00:00:56.256
"I don't see anyone."

19
00:00:56.276 --> 00:01:00.540
"It took me several zaps to unite with you earlier," Perda said.

20
00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:04.458
"Luckily Vilkor and Mellis didn't have much of a head start.

21
00:01:05.078 --> 00:01:07.280
I bet we'll catch up to them on the next zap."

22
00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.241
But she was wrong.

23
00:01:10.061 --> 00:01:13.423
It took three more zaps before they finally spotted Vilkor.

24
00:01:14.143 --> 00:01:17.365
He was surrounded by a small group of goons and other servants.

25
00:01:17.385 --> 00:01:19.547
"I wonder why they stopped here."

26
00:01:20.207 --> 00:01:23.029
Zann looked around at the wooded foothills where they'd landed.

27
00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.510
"There aren't any other people around."

28
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.732
Perda made sure that they were hidden behind some bushes.

29
00:01:29.988 --> 00:01:32.049
Then she sat down to catch her breath.

30
00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:35.069
"They probably stopped to rest," she said.

31
00:01:35.089 --> 00:01:36.070
"I'm glad.

32
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.410
I don't think we could have zapped any more today."

33
00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.431
"Where's Mellis?"

34
00:01:40.951 --> 00:01:41.671
Zann murmured.

35
00:01:42.331 --> 00:01:44.912
Just then Vilkor shouted, "Mellis!

36
00:01:45.072 --> 00:01:46.052
Where are you?"

37
00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:50.634
Mellis stepped into view from behind an extra-large goon.

38
00:01:51.274 --> 00:01:53.794
Perda was relieved to see that she looked okay.

39
00:01:54.875 --> 00:01:57.175
Vilkor pointed to a flat bit of ground.

40
00:01:57.195 --> 00:02:00.284
"Create my sleeping quarters here," he said.

41
00:02:00.304 --> 00:02:02.065
"Make sure it's comfortable.

42
00:02:02.185 --> 00:02:05.446
I want to be well rested when we arrive at the mountain village tomorrow."

43
00:02:06.166 --> 00:02:12.909
Mellis nodded and rubbed her hands together, quickly creating a large, luxurious tent with soft cushions inside.

44
00:02:13.569 --> 00:02:17.570
Next she created a table full of delicious-looking food and drink.

45
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.472
Zing noticed the food and tried to fly toward it, but Zann held him back.

46
00:02:23.672 --> 00:02:29.797
Perda watched Mellis create a comfortable lounge chair, which she magically placed next to the food table.

47
00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:31.818
"Wow," Perda whispered.

48
00:02:31.838 --> 00:02:35.201
"No wonder they were able to zap so far today.

49
00:02:35.962 --> 00:02:38.043
Mellis has a lot of power!"

50
00:02:38.063 --> 00:02:40.805
"I guess Zira was right," Zann said.

51
00:02:40.825 --> 00:02:44.909
"And I bet you were right when you said it's because Mellis was in the well when all

52
00:02:44.949 --> 00:02:46.550
that magic energy poured out."

53
00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:48.852
Perda nodded, feeling worried.

54
00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:55.062
If Zira knew how strong Mellis really was, she probably wouldn't let her remain free for long.

55
00:02:55.082 --> 00:02:58.342
"We need to get Mellis alone and talk to her."

56
00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:01.723
They didn't have a chance to do so for a while.

57
00:03:02.364 --> 00:03:06.965
While Vilkor lounged by the table, eating and drinking, he made Mellis work.

58
00:03:07.565 --> 00:03:11.446
He ordered her to make small, plain tents for the goons and servants.

59
00:03:12.086 --> 00:03:15.867
Then he told her to create an addition to his tent for herself.

60
00:03:15.887 --> 00:03:18.748
"Don't make it too big though," he said.

61
00:03:19.304 --> 00:03:21.185
"You don't want to wear yourself out.

62
00:03:22.026 --> 00:03:25.008
And what does a mere girl need with a lot of space?"

63
00:03:26.509 --> 00:03:27.830
Mellis nodded meekly.

64
00:03:28.531 --> 00:03:33.354
She snapped her fingers, and a smaller tent appeared, attached to Vilkor's large one.

65
00:03:33.895 --> 00:03:36.336
Meanwhile the goons were digging a fire pit.

66
00:03:37.177 --> 00:03:39.859
As darkness fell, they lit a campfire.

67
00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:42.641
Vilkor peered at it from his lounge chair.

68
00:03:42.661 --> 00:03:44.902
"Fetch more wood," he ordered.

69
00:03:44.922 --> 00:03:46.964
"We can't let the fire go out.

70
00:03:47.652 --> 00:03:49.594
I don't sleep well when it's chilly."

71
00:03:49.614 --> 00:03:53.857
"Doesn't he realize he could snap his fingers and make more wood?"

72
00:03:54.218 --> 00:03:54.918
Zann whispered.

73
00:03:54.938 --> 00:03:58.601
"Or he could create a fire that doesn't require wood to burn."

74
00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:00.663
Perda shrugged.

75
00:04:00.683 --> 00:04:04.806
"Vilkor still doesn't seem to understand how magic works.

76
00:04:05.587 --> 00:04:07.768
No wonder Zira can trick him so easily."

77
00:04:08.569 --> 00:04:13.013
She noticed two servants, a man and a woman, hiking into the woods nearby.

78
00:04:13.813 --> 00:04:18.849
She and Zann ducked down farther so they wouldn't be seen, holding Zing still between them.

79
00:04:19.529 --> 00:04:23.891
As the servants passed the kids' hiding place, one bent to grab a fallen branch.

80
00:04:24.571 --> 00:04:26.692
The second glanced back over her shoulder.

81
00:04:26.712 --> 00:04:30.393
"This is ridiculous," the woman whispered.

82
00:04:30.413 --> 00:04:37.736
"Vilkor and Zira claim that magic involves secret spells and that only certain people can do it.

83
00:04:38.437 --> 00:04:43.919
But I heard a rumor back in town that magic can be done by anyone and that it's

84
00:04:43.979 --> 00:04:45.339
not difficult at all!"

85
00:04:45.359 --> 00:04:49.337
"Really?" The male servant looked skeptical.

86
00:04:49.357 --> 00:04:51.037
"Who told you that?"

87
00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:54.179
"My friend Finna," the woman replied.

88
00:04:54.699 --> 00:04:55.859
Then she looked worried.

89
00:04:55.879 --> 00:04:58.861
"It was right before she disappeared.

90
00:04:59.461 --> 00:05:02.722
You don't think Zira did something to her, do you?"

91
00:05:03.863 --> 00:05:04.603
The man shrugged.

92
00:05:04.623 --> 00:05:06.664
"Who knows what Zira might do?"

93
00:05:07.564 --> 00:05:09.325
He lowered his voice even more.

94
00:05:09.345 --> 00:05:13.446
"But actually, my sister told me the same thing Finna told you.

95
00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:16.908
She heard it from a miner who'd just returned to the village.

96
00:05:17.496 --> 00:05:18.837
Do you think it could be true?"

97
00:05:19.577 --> 00:05:23.560
The pair moved farther into the woods until Perda couldn't hear them anymore.

98
00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.641
"Wow," she whispered.

99
00:05:26.121 --> 00:05:27.682
"I guess the truth is spreading!"

100
00:05:28.903 --> 00:05:35.026
Eventually Vilkor ate and drank so much that he fell asleep in the lounge chair, snoring loudly.

101
00:05:35.726 --> 00:05:38.448
The servants discussed whether to move him into the tent.

102
00:05:39.128 --> 00:05:40.609
Finally a goon shrugged.

103
00:05:41.049 --> 00:05:43.111
"Doesn't look like rain," he said.

104
00:05:43.131 --> 00:05:45.192
"Let's just get some rest."

105
00:05:46.044 --> 00:05:49.145
Everyone else crawled into their tents, including Mellis.

106
00:05:50.045 --> 00:05:53.686
Perda and Zann waited until they heard snores from all directions.

107
00:05:54.647 --> 00:05:59.468
Then they crawled cautiously past the sleeping Vilkor to Mellis' tent.

108
00:06:00.028 --> 00:06:03.910
Zing followed, sniffing in the direction of the mostly empty food table.

109
00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.010
"Zing, stop!"

110
00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:07.091
Zann whispered.

111
00:06:07.751 --> 00:06:11.472
But the little dragon had just spotted Mellis sleeping inside the tent.

112
00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.664
He rushed in and breathed hot air in her face, flapping his wings in greeting.

113
00:06:17.424 --> 00:06:19.086
Mellis sat up and rubbed her face.

114
00:06:19.826 --> 00:06:21.888
Her eyes widened when she saw Zing.

115
00:06:22.549 --> 00:06:25.971
She glanced at Perda and Zann, and her expression went dark.

116
00:06:26.792 --> 00:06:29.835
She pushed Zing away and shook her head angrily.
